# hk: fix vertex shader NIR leak and double free
# https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/46312 state=opened
# ### What does this MR do and why?

<!--Describe in detail what your merge request does and why.-->

```
hk: fix vertex shader NIR leak and double free

hk_compile_shader hands the original NIR to the last variant of a vertex or
tessellation evaluation shader instead of cloning it, and that variant frees
it. But "last" was hardcoded to the software variant, which is only compiled
when the shader may be used with geometry/tessellation. Without it, the
hardware variant compiles a clone and the original NIR is never freed, so
every vertex shader leaks its NIR.

Hand the original NIR to the last variant that is actually compiled. Also do
not free it a second time in the failure path of that variant, where the
clone is the original NIR and has already been freed.

Signed-off-by: s0ullight <opossum.pizazz-5h@icloud.com>
```
--- src/asahi/vulkan/hk_shader.c
+++ src/asahi/vulkan/hk_shader.c
